A||||3||82-T/A||Well, I finally figured out whats wrong with my Fiero...||||9||
Z||000000||82-T/A||12-02-2000||11:17 PM||||I finally figured out whats wrong with my car. It appears that when my waterpump went dead in my Fiero... my car overheated soo badly, that it seriously wore out my crank bearings. <P>I now have a rattling in the top end of my motor.. but it's only when the engine has warmed up. Here is what I've concluded.. tell me if it's wrong. <P>Becausemy oil pressure is SOOO low after the cars warmed up, that the valves aren't fully opening. Since the lifters are hydraulic, they require hydraulic fluid (oil) to opperate at full compression on the pushrods. If not.. they won't fully open the valves like they're supposed to. This would explain my problem with no power about 3,000 rpms. <P>So I've got to make a decision on what I need to do with this car. Obviously junking it is out of the question, and I can't sell it since it was my very first car that "I" actually bought... AND had the title in my name. <P>I guess my only choice is to rebuild, or replace. <P>The only problem I have with replacing the short block is that my engine is the original.. is there any way that I can remove the VIN tag off my engine and put it on the new motor? Is there any way that someone could tell? <P>What is a good price for a shortblock... hmm... 3.1? <P>May as well get the 3.1 since I'm going to do it anyway. <P>Do you guys see any problem with a Crane CompuCAM Camshaft from a 2.8 Fiero working in a 3.1? <P>EXACT same engine.. block is the same. The only thing thats different is the crank and pistons. <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Todd Jaspers<BR>1997 Pontiac GrandAm SE<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero SE/V6<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2m4 SE<BR>http://www.ezshots.com/album.cgi?82tafiero/Apartment||||reg||9
Z||000001||Phil||12-03-2000||06:25 AM||||This one is kinda easy. Just have your dead 2.8 rebuilt as a 3.1. All that has to be changed is the crank,pistons and if you have a pre 88 the flywheel. Same block for both engines.||||reg||1
Z||000002||RedOktober||12-05-2000||04:51 AM||||Hey what a small world... Thats exactly what happened to Red Oktober..Head Gasket Blew and got this annoying clicking noise from the lifters! The Crank is tapered and Grindable. But I have the same dilema. Depending on your budget, you should go for a good 2.8 rebuild with forged pistons, or a 3.1/3.4 rebuild or conversion.<P>------------------<BR>86 SE V6 Auto Turbo Going 3.4 OHV "Red Oktober"<BR>86 2M4 5sp (Beater) "Blackie"<BR>87 GT "Blue Flame"||||reg||1
Z||000003||82-T/A||12-05-2000||08:40 AM||||Yeah, I think I will. I'll rebuild my stock 2.8 into a 3.1 with a Competition Camshaft for more torque.<P>I've already ported my entire intake setup, and I have 1.52:1 Crane roller rockers and all the LITTLE bolt ons.<P>So the cam and the extra displacement should give me some decent power. Is it unrealisitic to say that I'd get around <BR>175hp and 210pounds of torque?<P>THe stock Fiero gets 170lbs of torque, and I hear that switching it to the 3.1 automatically brings it up to 160hp and 190lbs of torque. I was hoping the cam would bring it up just a little more.<P><P>------------------<BR>Todd Jaspers<BR>1997 Pontiac GrandAm SE<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero SE/V6<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2m4 SE<BR>http://www.ezshots.com/album.cgi?82tafiero/Apartment||||reg||1
